<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="unit4b-projects">
  <time minutes="90" />
  <title>Unit 4B Projects</title>
  <idx>projects</idx>

  <introduction>  
<p><em>
    These projects were created by Leigh Anne Fitz and Lisa Ferran to provide engaging, standards-aligned learning experiences for AP Computer Science A students.  The autograding tests were designed by Kate McDonnell.
</em></p>
<p>
Now that you've learned to work with arrays, it's time to explore ArrayLists—a flexible data structure that can grow and shrink as your program runs. In these projects, you'll learn how to create and manipulate ArrayList objects, access and update elements, add and remove items, and develop algorithms that process dynamic collections of data.  
</p>
<p>
  Each project is designed to reinforce these concepts through authentic programming tasks. As you complete them, focus on selecting the appropriate ArrayList methods, using loops to process collections efficiently, and carefully managing element positions as data is added or removed. Mastering ArrayLists will help you build programs that are more adaptable and better suited for managing real-world data.
</p>
  </introduction>

<subsection xml:id="unit4b-project1">
<title>Unit 4B Project 1 - Remove Duplicates</title>

  
<activity label="unit4b-project1-remove-duplicates">
<statement>
<p>
      Create a program that will remove duplicate values from an ArrayList.  In the main method, create an ArrayList of Integers.  Fill the ArrayList with 20 random Integers in the range 1 to 10 using a for loop.  Print your ArrayList with all values on one line with a space between them using a for loop.  Write a static method called removeDuplicates that will receive your ArrayList as a parameter and return the ArrayList with all duplicate values removed.  The method should also print out the values that it is removing as they are being removed.  You are to do this with nested for loops (use i and j as your loop variables).  Remember to think about what happens with your index values when you remove an element.  Back in main, print out the ArrayList returned by the method.     
</p>
<p>
  Example:
</p>

<pre>
Original list:  3 5 1 2 3 9 10 10 7 1 3 4 8 10 7 5 2 6 4 2
Removed:  3
Removed:  3
Removed:  5
Removed:  1
Removed:  2
Removed:  2
Removed:  10
Removed:  10
Removed:  7
Removed:  4
List without Duplicates:  3 5 1 2 9 10 7 4 8 6
</pre>

</statement>
<program interactive="activecode" language="java">
<code>
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {

  }

  // This code will not compile until you create your removeDuplicates method header
  
}
</code>
<tests>
import static org.junit.Assert.*;
import org.junit.*;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class RunestoneTests extends CodeTestHelper {
    public RunestoneTests() {
        super("Main");
    }

    @Test
    public void test01() {
        String expected = "ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected)) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }

            passed = stringMatch(actual, "new " + expected + "()")
                    || stringMatch(actual, "new ArrayList&lt;&gt;()");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        expected = expected + " * = new " + expected + "()";
        getResults(replaceTags(expected), replaceTags(actual), "ArrayList of Integers created properly", passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test02() {
        String expected = "Math.random()";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected)) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }

            boolean cast = stringMatch(actual, "(int)");
            boolean shift = stringMatch(actual, "+1");
            boolean range = stringMatch(actual, "*10");

            passed = cast &amp;&amp; shift &amp;&amp; range;
            actual += "Cast: " + cast + "\nRange: " + range + "\nShift: " + shift;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        String expect = "Cast: true\nRange: true\nShift: true";

        getResults(expect, actual, "Math.random() used to create an integer in the range [1, 10]", passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test03() {
        String expected = "for";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");
            code = getMethodCode(code, "for");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            boolean loop = false;

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected) &amp;&amp; line.contains("20")) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                    loop = true;
                } else if (loop &amp;&amp; line.contains(".add(")) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                    break;
                }
            }

            passed = stringMatch(actual, "for (int") &amp;&amp; actual.contains("++") &amp;&amp; actual.contains(".add(");
            boolean pass2 = stringMatch(actual, "= 0") &amp;&amp; stringMatch(actual, "&lt; 20");
            boolean pass3 = stringMatch(actual, "= 1") &amp;&amp; stringMatch(actual, "&lt;= 20");
            boolean pass4 = pass2 || pass3;
            passed = passed &amp;&amp; pass4;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        expected = "for(int i = 0; i &lt; 20; i++)";
        getResults(expected, actual, "20 random integers are added to the ArrayList using a for loop", passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test04() {

        String expected = "removeDuplicates";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected) &amp;&amp; line.contains("public")) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }
            passed = stringMatch(actual, expected);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        expected = "public static ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; removeDuplicates(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;";

        getResults(replaceTags(expected + " *)"), replaceTags(actual), "Header for removeDuplicates method is correct",
                passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test05() {
        String desc = "Nested for loops used to traverse arrays";
        String expected = "for";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();

            code = getMethodCode(code, "public static ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;");
            // System.out.println(code);

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected)) {
                    actual += line.trim() + "\n";
                }
            }

            int fors = countOccurences(actual, "for");
            int size = countOccurences(actual, ".size()");

            String forwardStr = "for\\(int([a-zA-Z0-9_]+)=(0|[a-zA-Z0-9_]+\\+1);\\1&lt;[a-zA-Z0-9_]+.size\\(\\)[-1]*;\\1\\+\\+\\)\\{*";
            String backwardStr = "for\\(int([a-zA-Z0-9_]+)=[a-zA-Z0-9_\\.\\(\\)]*-1;\\1&gt;=*[a-zA-Z0-9]*;\\1--\\)\\{*";

            String[] loops = actual.split("\n");
            int numLoops = loops.length;

            int forward = 0, backward = 0;

            if (numLoops == 2) {
                for (String line : loops) {
                    // System.out.println(line);
                    if (line.replaceAll(" ", "").matches(forwardStr)) {
                        // System.out.println(line + " --&gt; forward");
                        forward++;
                    }

                    if (line.replaceAll(" ", "").matches(backwardStr)) {
                        // System.out.println(line + " --&gt; backward");
                        backward++;
                    }
                }
            }

            passed = forward + backward == 2;

        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Test caused an exception";
        }

        expected = "for(int i = 0; i &lt; d.size(); i++)\n" +
                "for(int j = i + 1; j &lt; d.size(); j++)\n\n";
        getResults(expected, actual, desc, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test06() {
        String desc = "if statement used for comparison of two data elements";
        String expected = "if";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "public static ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected)) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }

            passed = countOccurences(actual, ".get(") == 2 &amp;&amp; actual.contains("==");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Test caused an exception";
        }

        expected = "if (*.get(*) == *.get(*))";
        getResults(expected, actual, desc, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test07() {
        String desc = "System.out.print used at least twice to print elements from list in main method";
        String expected = "System.out.print(";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected) &amp;&amp; line.contains(".get")) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }

            passed = actual.split("\n").length &gt;= 2;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Test caused an exception";
        }

        expected = "System.out.print(*.get(*));\nSystem.out.print(*.get(*));";
        getResults(expected, actual, desc, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test08() {
        String desc = "System.out.println used at least once to print elements as they are removed in removeDuplicates method";
        String expected = "System.out.print";
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        try {
            String code = getCode();
            code = getMethodCode(code, "public static ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;");

            String[] lines = code.split("\n");

            for (String line : lines) {
                if (line.contains(expected)) {
                    actual += line + "\n";
                }
            }

            passed = actual.contains(".get(") || actual.contains(".remove(");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Test caused an exception";
            passed = false;
        }

        expected = "System.out.println(*.get(*)); // or\nSystem.out.println(*.remove(*));";
        getResults(expected, actual, desc, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test09() {
        ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; expect = new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;(Arrays.asList(10, 1, 4, 2, 5, 6, 7));
        String expected = expect.toString();
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; list1 = new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;(
                Arrays.asList(10, 1, 4, 4, 2, 1, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7, 5, 10, 5, 1, 4, 1, 10, 6, 6));
        String list = list1.toString();

        try {
            ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; result = Main.removeDuplicates(list1);
            actual = result.toString();

            passed = result.equals(expect);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        getResults(expected, actual, "Testing with values " + list, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    @Test
    public void test10() {
        ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; expect = new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;(Arrays.asList(3, 7, 8, 6, 4, 9, 1, 5, 10));
        String expected = expect.toString();
        String actual = "";
        boolean passed = false;

        ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; list1 = new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;(
                Arrays.asList(3, 3, 7, 8, 3, 7, 6, 4, 9, 9, 9, 1, 8, 4, 9, 3, 5, 1, 1, 10));
        String list = list1.toString();

        try {
            ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; result = Main.removeDuplicates(list1);
            actual = result.toString();

            passed = result.equals(expect);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            actual = "Error";
            passed = false;
        }

        getResults(expected, actual, "Testing with values " + list, passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }

    private String getMethodCode(String code, String name) {
        String searchStr = code;
        int start = searchStr.indexOf(name);
        searchStr = searchStr.substring(start);

        int level = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i &lt; searchStr.length(); i++) {
            if (searchStr.substring(i, i + 1).equals("{")) {
                level++;
            } else if (searchStr.substring(i, i + 1).equals("}")) {
                level--;

                if (level == 0) {
                    // System.out.println(searchStr.substring(0, i+1).trim());
                    return searchStr.substring(0, i + 1).trim();
                }
            }
        }

        return searchStr.trim();
    }

    private boolean stringMatch(String str1, String str2) {
        str1 = str1.replaceAll(" ", "");
        str2 = str2.replaceAll(" ", "");

        return str1.contains(str2);
    }

    private String replaceTags(String str) {
        return str.replaceAll("&gt;", "&amp;gt;").replaceAll("&lt;", "&amp;lt;");
    }
}
   
</tests>
</program>
</activity>

</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="unit4b-project2">
<title>Unit 4B Project 2 - ArrayList Operations</title>

<activity label="unit4b-project2-arraylist-operations">
<statement>
<p>
  Create a program that utilizes common ArrayList algorithms. In main, create an ArrayList of Integers.  Use a for loop to fill the ArrayList with 50 random Integers in the range 0 to 100.  Create static methods to return the following values:
</p>
